					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/caulf1eld" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5994099); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5994099&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607847090" alt="Caulf1eld" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5994099)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/caulf1eld" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5994099); return false;" >Caulf1eld</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607837823 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Dec 2020 05:37</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843521">
									

<p>Alright, so I just made some revisions to this thing and tried to make some improvements to the central narrative part of this thing.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Central&nbsp;narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Central&nbsp;narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>They go into hiding in a forest after abandoning the nazi cause and uses their anomalous capability, guns, utilities, etc, to survive in the wilderness and avoid capture. As time goes on, dissidence begins to grow in each of them against the former regime they served.</p>
<p>During a containment breach at a nearby facility, a massive sinkhole is formed taking the tank along with her crew with it to the bottom. They survive the fall but find themselves in a world similar to our own, a damp, dark, cold world lacking any source of light. As the group ventures throughout this “underworld,” they discover that it’s populated entirely by dark, shadowy beings that bear a disfigured, grainy, slender silhouette of a human. Worst yet is that they seem to be on the hunt for the tank crew.</p>
<p>Looking for a way out and forced to survive in this new world against these creatures, the tank crew utilize what limited ammunition and supply they have left on them to ensure the safety of their survival. Eventually, the tank that they utilized began to slowly change, with deep scratch marks being discovered both inside and outside the tank. The tank crew were ready to abandon the tank thinking that it was beginning to wear down until the radio man discovered that using the radio at a certain frequency would spawn a massive WWII era german tank army filled with mighty caliber guns capable of toppling the deadliest war machines ever built, and armour that were incapable of penetration.</p>
<p>It would only be decades later when the group would return to our world with their hand in the air, surrounded by SCP agents during an investigation into the sinkhole. When reappearing from the underworld, the tank crew would utilize their tank army as a show of defiance against their new captors, only to realize that the former tank army that was made of the toughest armour had become a hazy, transparent division. Objects would come and go through the ghost tanks, causing little harm as the screams of horrors by soldiers being gunned down and mutilated would play as they rolled past, deafening the roaring engines of the tanks.</p>
<p>The tank crew would eventually be captured and held in captivity by SCP researchers putting an end to their escape. Days later, ghosts of tanks would appear throughout Europe and North Africa, firing upon civilian homes, shopping centres, gas stations and random buildings leaving destruction and tens to hundreds of casualties with zero traces of the ghosts left. An interview conducted on the tank crew would show similarities in both their journey in the underworld and the aforementioned incident in terms of behaviour, actions and locations.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>It's a lot to take in but it's my attempt at improving it, giving it some kind of story to it and just being my first SCP in general</p>
<p>Criticisms and critiques would be appreciated</p>

